            "icon": "",
            "icon_size": "large",
            "heading": "A Living Gallery",
            "content": "<p>I've built <strong>30 hand-crafted visual styles</strong> into the ABD theme. Each one is a complete aesthetic experience:<br/><br/><em><strong>- Cable News</strong></em> – Breaking news urgency with ticker-tape energy<br/><br/>- <em><strong>California Mission</strong></em> – Adobe warmth and Spanish colonial elegance  <br/><br/>- <em><strong>Cubism</strong></em> – Fragmented geometry meets Picasso-inspired layouts<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Disco</strong></em> – Glitter, groove, and Studio 54 maximalism<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Impressionist</strong></em> – Monet-soft colors and painterly textures<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Millennial MySpace</strong></em> – Y2K nostalgia with customizable chaos<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Retro Internet </strong></em>– GeoCities boxes, under-construction GIFs, and web 1.0 charm<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Las Vegas</strong></em> – Neon grids, outrun aesthetics, and 80s futurism<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Zine</strong></em> – Cut-and-paste punk energy with DIY collage vibes<br/><br/>Instead of generic \"light\" and \"dark\" modes, I wanted <strong>cultural moments as design systems</strong>. The idea is that a store can switch its entire personality in seconds—from Renaissance oil painting to highway street photography.</p>",
            "link_text": "Terms of Service",
            "link_url": "shopify://pages/terms-of-service",
            "show_link_arrow": true,
            "custom_html": ""
          }
        },
        "feature_jzVkJw": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "",
            "icon_size": "large",
            "heading": "Art First, Commerce Second",
            "content": "<p>Most Shopify themes are built for conversion optimization. I built ABD for <strong>creative expression.<br/></strong><em><strong><br/>What makes it different<br/><br/></strong></em><em>No \"</em><em><strong>best practices</strong></em><em>\" constraints</em><br/> Layouts break grids, text overlaps images, colors clash intentionally<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Anti-corporate aesthetic</strong></em> –<br/> I rejected the sterile minimalism of modern e-commerce for bold, opinionated design<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Cultural references over trends</strong></em> – <br/>Drawing from art history, subcultures, and forgotten eras instead of following what's popular<br/><br/>- <em><strong>Personality over polish</strong></em> – <br/>Embracing imperfection, texture, and character<br/><br/>I didn't ask \"will this convert?\" <br/><br/>I asked \"<em><strong>will this be remembered?</strong></em>\"</p>",
            "link_text": "Privacy Policy",
            "link_url": "shopify://pages/privacy",
            "show_link_arrow": true,
            "custom_html": ""
          }
        },
        "feature_GRGnNJ": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "",
            "icon_size": "large",
            "heading": "Build Like an Artist",
            "content": "<p>The block architecture lets me <strong>compose pages like collages</strong>:<br/><br/><em><strong>Feature Blocks</strong></em><br/> Icon + text combinations with theme-specific styling<br/><br/><em><strong>Image & Text Blocks</strong></em><br/>Asymmetric layouts that break the 50/50 grid<br/><br/><em><strong>Badge Blocks</strong></em><br/>Stickers, stamps, and labels with retro positioning<br/><br/><em><strong>Custom HTML Blocks</strong></em><br/>Full creative freedom for experimental layouts<br/><br/><em><strong>Accordion Blocks</strong></em><br/>Expandable content with theme-aware animations<br/><br/>Each block inherits the active ABD style, so a \"Disco\" button looks completely different from a \"California Mission\" button—<strong>same content, 30 different artistic interpretations</strong>.<br/><br/>I wanted pages that feel hand-designed, not template-generated.</p>",
            "link_text": "Return and Refund Policy",
            "link_url": "shopify://pages/return-and-refund-policy",
            "show_link_arrow": true,
            "custom_html": ""
          }
        },
        "feature_KRaPat": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "",
            "icon_size": "large",
            "heading": "Cultural Time Travel",
            "content": "<p>ABD doesn't just style a store it <strong>transports it to another era or movement</strong>.<br/><br/><em><strong>Examples of what I built:<br/></strong></em><br/>- <em>Renaissance</em> – Ornate borders, classical typography, museum-quality presentation<br/><br/>- <em>Newspaper</em> – Columns, mastheads, and print journalism layouts<br/><br/>- <em>National Parks Poster</em> – WPA-era screen printing and vintage travel aesthetics<br/><br/>- <em>Free Love</em> – Psychedelic swirls, peace signs, and 60s counterculture<br/><br/>- <em>Military Theme</em> – Stenciled fonts, olive drab, and utilitarian design<br/><br/>-<em>Valentines</em> – Romantic pinks, hearts, and love letter elegance<br/><br/>Each style isn't just a color palette—it's a <strong>complete design language</strong> with custom fonts, layout rules, and decorative elements that make a store feel like it belongs in a specific time and place.<br/><br/>This is the only Shopify theme where a store can look like a 1950s diner menu, a 1990s GeoCities page, or a French Impressionist painting—<br/><br/><em><strong>all from the same codebase</strong></em>.</p>",
